.el .ds Aq '
.TH tensor-wasm-man 1  "tensor-wasm-man "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-man \- Generate roff(7) man pages from the clap command tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm man\fR [\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR=\fIOUT_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Walks the clap \fBCommand\fR tree, renders one \fB.1\fR page per node via \fBclap_mangen::Man\fR, and writes the resulting groff sources either to a caller\-supplied directory or to stdout (root page only). Used to regenerate the committed scaffolding under \fBcrates/tensor-wasm-cli/man/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR=\fIOUT_DIR\fR
Output directory. When omitted, only the root \fBtensor-wasm.1\fR page is emitted to stdout. When provided, every subcommand gets its own page written as \fB<binary>-<subcommand>.1\fR (matching the established convention used by \fBgit-status(1)\fR, \fBcargo-build(1)\fR, etc.).
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id (inherited from the top\-level flag; unused by this subcommand).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
# Regenerate every committed man page in one pass
tensor\-wasm man \-\-out\-dir crates/tensor-wasm-cli/man

# Pipe the root page to stdout for ad\-hoc preview
tensor\-wasm man | man \-l \-
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-completions(1)
